  "question": {
    "text": "The least positive integer $\\mathrm{n}$ such that $1-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{3^2}-\\ldots .-\\frac{2}{3^{n-1}} < \\frac{1}{100}$, is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n4\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n5\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n6\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n7",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&1-\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{3^2} \\ldots \\cdot \\frac{2}{3^{n-1}} < \\frac{1}{100} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow 1-\\frac{2}{3}\\left[\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3^2}+\\frac{1}{3^3}+\\ldots \\frac{1}{3^{n-1}}\\right] < \\frac{1}{100} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow \\frac{1-2\\left[\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\frac{1}{3^n}-1\\right)\\right]}{\\frac{1}{3}-1} < \\frac{1}{100} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow 1-2\\left[\\frac{3^n-1}{2.3^n}\\right] < \\frac{1}{100} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow 1-\\left[\\frac{3^n-1}{3^n}\\right] < \\frac{1}{100} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow 1-1+\\frac{1}{3^n} < \\frac{1}{100}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\Rightarrow 100 < 3^n\n$$\nThus, least value of $n$ is 5"
  }
}